WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.659 --> 00:00:05.970
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and these are
going to be my Korra Book 4 predictions. The

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:10.450
good news is that Mike and Bryan said that
pretty much every major character and storyline

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:15.190
gets dealt with by the end. As of right now
there isn’t an official release date but

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:20.420
plan for Summer next year until they say otherwise.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:27.420
It will stream for free everywhere it is right
now. But let’s get going. Careful for spoilers

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:31.550
from the finale if you haven’t seen it yet.
I’ll wait just a sec...Okay, starting with

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:35.770
number 10 - There will be no Korra presence
at Comic Con next summer.

00:00:35.770 --> 00:00:39.629
Mostly because they’ll probably release
it before then. The Second big reason is because

00:00:39.629 --> 00:00:43.809
if they barely spent any time or energy marketing
it this year and they’ve already written

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:48.399
the cost of producing it off. They already
paid for all the episodes to be made. Why

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:52.750
bother spending the extra money to rent out
ballroom 20 and bring the cast out.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:55.329
If you want to do a panel at comic con you
have to pay money and if you want a booth

00:00:55.329 --> 00:00:58.920
on the floor it’s crazy expensive.

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:02.960
Mike and Bryan said during the comic con panel
this year for book 3 that they expected it

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.940
was their last time at San Diego Comic Con
for Korra.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.610
They will be at New York Comic Con this fall.
That’s October 9th to 12th. I won’t be

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:17.310
there, but I will be doing videos for any
big stuff that happens.

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:24.310
Number 9 - Book 4 will be the last Avatar
Series, there will be no Movie but the Comics

00:01:29.569 --> 00:01:30.550
will keep going

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:33.539
Mike and Bryan said that they were pretty
fried on the Avatar Universe after spending

00:01:33.539 --> 00:01:38.060
the last 10 years of their life working on
it. They will continue to develop new shows,

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:41.660
probably animated shows. But they won’t
be Avatar related.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:46.800
The big asterisk is nothing is every confirmed
in Hollywood. People quit stuff all the time

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:52.550
and then a dump truck of money rolls up and
all of a sudden it’s a thing again. So more

00:01:52.550 --> 00:01:55.880
Avatar video is up to Nick. Which is unlikely.

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:59.489
But the comics will totally keep going, they’re
way easier to produce and they have a lot

00:01:59.489 --> 00:02:01.890
more freedom with what they can do. So more
Last Airbender and Korra Stories via the comics.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:05.440
Also there are video games coming right now.
Depending on the success of those, there will

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:06.160
be more games.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:10.590
I know everyone wants an animated movie and
a billion more seasons. But Bryke basically

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:13.500
said on the podcast he did that he doesn’t
want to do that.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.760
Which leads to Number 8 - The Book 4 Finale
will end in a way that allows the Avatar Cycle

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:19.930
to continue even if it’s not on screen

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:24.260
There is no way any of their writing or belief
systems have led me to believe that Korra

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:29.720
will be the Last Avatar ever. That whole idea
was a major plot point of the Book 3 finale.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:34.000
Zaheer thought the world didn’t need the
Avatar anymore, but Tenzin clearly states

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.240
evidence as to why they need an Avatar more
than ever.

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.720
The Line will continue. We just don't’ know
if Korra will survive the finale or if we’ll

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.800
see her live to old age.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.270
What I’d like to see whether or not they
choose to do it, is for the final scene to

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:49.650
be something close to Avatar Wan’s final
scene in Beginnings. Where Korra is dying

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:54.100
in old age in the middle of a battle or even
just at home with her family and we hear a

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:56.180
baby cry out as she fades away.

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.040
Just a way to imply that 1, the avatar cycle
is continuing and 2, there is still imbalance

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.480
in the world, everyone still needs an Avatar.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.230
I would like to see a flashforward or at least
some acknowledgement that Korra got some of

00:03:05.230 --> 00:03:06.750
the things she wanted in life.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:11.490
I understand if they chose not to do that
in an explicit way. Sometimes that’s too

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:15.480
on the nose and it’s more effective to just
imply that the cycle will continue regardless

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.860
of what’s going on in the world.

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:24.860
Avatar is all about cycles. Harmonic Convergence,
Raava and Vaatu, the 100 year war and now

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:30.600
the collapse of the Earth Kingdom. Everything
gets repeated, so I’d at least like to see

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.940
an ending that fits with that thematically.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.350
On to Number 7 - Jinora is going to follow
a more enlightened version of the path that

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.800
Aang and Korra went on.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:44.830
I don’t think they’ll copy and paste Aang’s
character development on to her. But she is

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:48.950
a child burdened with the leadership of the
Air Nation, so you can’t help but point

00:03:48.950 --> 00:03:54.390
to Aang. The difference is that she has his
level of spirituality with Korra’s gung

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:59.560
ho attitude. So it’s like she all of their
best qualities.

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:06.560
I think the series is positioning her to be
the next non-Avatar World Leader. Like she’ll

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:15.040
be the new Iroh and probably go on to lead
the white lotus along with the Air Nation

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.709
for the rest of her life.

00:04:16.709 --> 00:04:21.720
Avatar Yangchen is the best example of a female
air master. So think of Jinora as living out

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:22.410
a life similar to that.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:26.380
Number 6 - All the major characters will be
back

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:33.380
That includes Katara, Zuko, Toph, all off
the Team Aang characters that are still alive.

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:40.490
The major conflict is the revolution that
the Red Lotus is trying to start. Zaheer said

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:44.810
that it had started but as far as we know
that’s only in the Earth Kingdom.

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:48.600
I think they’ll continue to use the original
Last Airbender characters the same way they

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:55.600
used Zuko in book 3. As support for Team Korra.
Lots of unanswered questions about where Toph

00:04:56.150 --> 00:05:00.820
and Azula have been since last we saw them.
Because Bryke said they tie everything up.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.880
I think it at least means we’ll get an answer.
Maybe not the answer we want, but something

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.060
is better than nothing.

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:09.419
Number 5 - Korrasami will still be a thing

00:05:09.419 --> 00:05:14.440
I know a lot of you ask me my thoughts on
korrasami. I love the two of them together

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:20.750
but I don’t think there’s anything sexual
going on. They just wanted Korra and Asami

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:24.820
to have a positive female friend that didn’t
have anything to do with boyfriends.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:29.580
Yes they do share Mako in common, but he’s
the only one at this point that’s still

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:35.389
weird about it. With all that Korra has been
through I’m expecting Asami to stay and

00:05:35.389 --> 00:05:38.650
help take care of her until she’s fully
healed.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:45.650
During last airbender Aang had to heal the
avatar spirit by reconnecting with his past

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:52.790
lives in the spirit realm. I know they’ve
retconned a few things, because at the time

00:05:55.770 --> 00:06:00.830
those episodes aired. Mike and Bryan hadn’t
incorporated the idea of Raava, Vaatu and

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:05.669
Avatar Wan into the series. So there were
only a handful of Avatar spirits he had to

00:06:05.669 --> 00:06:05.889
visit.

00:06:05.889 --> 00:06:09.710
Korra is still cut off from all her past lives.
But unless they change things again there’s

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:11.919
always Yangchen’s Festival. I know a few
of you have asked me about this on a couple

00:06:11.919 --> 00:06:11.960
videos.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:16.180
Which should make you guys excited for Number
4 - Korra will reconnect with her past lives

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.729
I know Mike and Bryan did an interview after
book 2 ended saying Korra would continue to

00:06:19.729 --> 00:06:24.350
be cut off. But I think it’s possible they
could have just been talking about Book 3.

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:29.790
The Yangchen Festival method comes straight
from The Rift Part 2. That was written by

00:06:29.790 --> 00:06:35.460
Mike and Bryan and published just last month.
So it’s way more current than their earlier

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:39.080
comments about Korra being cut off.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:43.780
That happens all the time, where a creator
does an interview and teases something that

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:44.860
gets taken too literally.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:48.919
What is Yangchen’s Festival? This is where
it gets more exciting. It’s an Air Nomad

00:06:48.919 --> 00:06:54.449
festival started by Avatar Yangchen, the female
airbender I said Jinora is going to resemble.

00:06:54.449 --> 00:06:58.199
Airbenders are back, which means they’ll
celebrate Yangchen’s festival again in book

00:06:58.199 --> 00:07:03.800
4. Which gives Korra a backdoor for reconnecting
with her past lives.

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:08.229
Yangchen started the Festival as a way to
uphold a treaty with the ancient spirit of

00:07:08.229 --> 00:07:13.979
Old General Iroh. Not Uncle Iroh, someone
who was way way older. the Festival continued

00:07:13.979 --> 00:07:16.710
after her death as a way for the air nation
to honor her achievements.

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:19.650
They don’t really explain the physics of
how participating in the festival facilitates

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:22.830
the reconnection of past lives. But I take
them at their word.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:26.710
If you’ve listened to the Book 2 dvd commentaries.
Sometimes Mike and Bryan fudge the logic of

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:27.820
situations. Like Jinora pulling Raava out
of Unavaatu. They didn’t get really granular

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:29.590
the opportunity to speak with Aang and the
other avatars again.

00:07:29.590 --> 00:07:31.880
On to Number 3 - None of the Previous Villains
will be the problem of book 4

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:36.300
Zaheer won’t escape and be the big bad again,
Unalaq and Amon are dead but The Red Lotus

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:40.770
is still around. I don’t see them as being
the big bad though. I think the real villain

00:07:40.770 --> 00:07:45.850
will just be chaos itself and the air nomads.
As Tenzin said, will just travel from nation

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:48.280
to nation and help make things zen again.

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:55.280
There’s also the x-factor of Varrick and
his high speed rail. I think part of healing

00:07:56.090 --> 00:08:00.240
the world is bringing it closer together.
And the fastest way to do that is to create

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:04.139
high speed travel between cities. It’s like
the advent of the internet making the real

00:08:04.139 --> 00:08:05.910
world smaller so to speak.

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:11.080
I can post a youtube video and instantly all
over the world anywhere there’s internet

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.900
people can watch it at the same moment.

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:16.940
So I think Jinora and the air nation will
be like the spiritual solution and Varrick

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:21.919
will be the practical solution. Plus, if he
can establish a monopoly on shipping he’ll

00:08:21.919 --> 00:08:26.340
get even richer, which sounds like something
he would do. So he gets rich and gets to help

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:31.110
people. Although that part he probably doesn’t
care about so much.

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:36.619
Number 2 - Worldwide democracy will be a goal

00:08:36.619 --> 00:08:40.659
I think the things that Souyin talked about
while they were still with the Metal Clan

00:08:40.659 --> 00:08:44.169
will start to spread. Those ideas for equal
representation.

00:08:44.169 --> 00:08:49.170
When you look at the governments of all the
bending tribes the Fire Nation and the Water

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:49.929
Tribe are still the only ones that have acting
monarchs. And technically Korra’s father

00:08:49.929 --> 00:08:54.119
is more of an elected leader than the feudalistic
structure of the Fire Nation. They will be

00:08:54.119 --> 00:08:54.980
the last holdouts.

00:08:54.980 --> 00:09:01.369
Which is where Zuko’s daughter comes in.
As of right now the Fire Nation has been conspicuously

00:09:01.369 --> 00:09:06.119
absent with the exception of Zuko’s grandson
Iroh. He’s a general in the United Forces.

00:09:06.119 --> 00:09:10.980
So technically the Fire Nation didn’t contribute
any help in books 1 and 2, at least that we

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:11.839
saw.

00:09:11.839 --> 00:09:18.839
So I think that part of the move toward balance
will be the fire nation royal family giving

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:22.649
a lot of it’s legislative power away like
the royal family in England.

00:09:22.649 --> 00:09:26.300
In England the royal family is more of a figurehead
at this point and the day to day job of running

00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:30.939
the country falls on the government.

00:09:30.939 --> 00:09:35.429
And my number 1 prediction - Azula will also
be back

00:09:35.429 --> 00:09:39.059
She hasn’t been confirmed dead, the last
time we saw her was in the Search Comic and

00:09:39.059 --> 00:09:43.819
she was traveling with Team Avatar. She was
still totally nuts, but just like Toph. I

00:09:43.819 --> 00:09:46.999
think we’ll at least get a flashback.

00:09:46.999 --> 00:09:53.480
I fully expect all the notable characters
to be around when the series ends. Think about

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:58.459
it this way. You start with everyone together,
then circumstances draw them further and further

00:09:58.459 --> 00:10:02.050
apart till new circumstances pull them back
together. It’s like you have a single Avatar

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:03.329
Book that binds the original series and Legend
of Korra together. As Korra’s story has

00:10:03.329 --> 00:10:04.499
been told. you open the book and you have
last airbender people on one side of the page

00:10:04.499 --> 00:10:05.540
and the new team korra people on the other
side.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:08.199
Logically by the end of the story the book
has to be closed, bringing both the old characters

00:10:08.199 --> 00:10:09.699
and the new ones together.

00:10:09.699 --> 00:10:15.179
That’s the perfect situation, of course
the alternative is that all out mass hysteria

00:10:15.179 --> 00:10:20.279
and war could bring everyone back together.
Azula could always sieze on the new revolution

00:10:20.279 --> 00:10:23.670
to try and ursurp control of the fire nation.
She does have a claim to the throne.

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:28.699
At this point though, she’s a little bit
younger than Zuko, so she’d still be a very

00:10:28.699 --> 00:10:29.829
formidable warrior.

00:10:29.829 --> 00:10:35.889
Wouldn’t it be cool to see Old Katara and
Old Azula throw down. I’m not expecting

00:10:35.889 --> 00:10:37.759
anything like that but it’s fun to fantasize
about.

00:10:37.759 --> 00:10:42.480
But let me know what your predictions are
do you think that Toph and Azula will reappear

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:46.329
and do you think that Korra will reconnect
with her past lives?

00:10:46.329 --> 00:10:48.999
So busy weekend. Korra is going away for a
little while and Doctor Who is coming. I will

00:10:48.999 --> 00:10:52.199
be doing a Korra Q&amp;A, hopefully I’ll have
that up tonight. There’s also a video I’m

00:10:52.199 --> 00:10:54.920
working on based on a big interview Mike and
Bryan did, but that might take a few more

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.749
days to finish. I will be doing new Korra
next week.

00:10:56.749 --> 00:11:00.509
I also think there are a few giveaways running
right now, I’m catching up. There is definitely

00:11:00.509 --> 00:11:03.410
a weekly Doctor Who giveaway, so even if you
don’t like Doctor Who you should check out

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:03.939
those videos. I will be posting one shortly.

00:11:03.939 --> 00:11:06.589
But Right now click here for my Korra Finale
video and click here for the Q&amp;A, I’ll add

00:11:06.589 --> 00:11:09.239
the annotation as soon as I post it.

00:11:09.239 --> 00:11:13.170
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.
High Fives!

